 "honest": [
  "the era signs are identical at every band because a deadband cannot reach a level -- four rows of the same sign are one finding, not four",
  "a rate that moves while months_outside_deadband collapses is the band choosing its sample; a rate quoted with fewer than 6 months is labelled thin and kept out of the span",
  "the zero band reproduces the raw rate exactly, so E169's published figures remain readable inside this face",
  "sweeping a constant that was declared before the burn is a sensitivity table on a published reading, not a re-fit: nothing here selects a band",
  "descriptive census only: no gate, no verdict on the book, no prereg, no trial count"
